From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000
Subject: Write a dirty root's GlobalTransform only when its value changes
Date: 2026-11-26T12:04:58+00:00

propagate_parent_transforms visits every root whose tree changed and wrote
its GlobalTransform from its Transform unconditionally. That marked the
root's global changed even when its value was the same, so every direct
child failed the static scene check (neither its tree nor its parent's
global changed) and recomputed. A scene root at Genesis Plaza has about
600 direct children, so one moved leaf cost 600 multiplies.

The root is now written with set_if_neq, as descendants already are. A
global that was just added still reads as changed, so its children still
propagate; an orphan or a root with a stale global gets a value that
differs, so it is written. The serial (no_std) version passes an explicit
changed flag to its children instead of reading the change tick, so it is
left as it is.

The tests in plugins.rs also check that no pass marks a hierarchy global
changed without changing its value, and orphan a node with descendants.
---
